    "title": "Senior Human Resources Officer",
    "organization": "Shobole Electromechanical",
    "description": "Company Description Shobole Electromechanical is committed to elevating the standards of the elevator industry through innovative and reliable electromechanical solutions. The company focuses on delivering high-quality products and services that enhance safety, performance, and efficiency for clients. With a dedication to technical excellence, Shobole Electromechanical strives to be a trusted partner for modern vertical transportation needs. Team members collaborate in a professional environment that values innovation, reliability, and customer satisfaction. Role Description The Senior Human Resources Officer is a full-time, on-site role based in Addis Ababa. This role is responsible for overseeing HR operations, including the development and implementation of HR policies, procedures, and programs aligned with organizational goals. Daily tasks include managing employee relations, guiding performance management processes, supporting recruitment and onboarding, and ensuring accurate job descriptions and role profiles. The Senior Human Resources Officer will also advise managers on HR best practices, maintain HR records, support training and development initiatives, and ensure compliance with applicable labor regulations. This position collaborates closely with leadership to build a positive, inclusive, and high-performing workplace culture. Qualifications Strong Human Resources (HR) and HR Management skills, including experience leading HR operations and initiatives. Ability to develop, implement, and maintain HR Policies that support organizational objectives and compliance. Proficiency in Employee Relations, including conflict resolution, counseling, and promoting a respectful work environment. Experience in Job Description Development and role profiling to support recruitment, performance management, and career paths. Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Management, or a related field; advanced HR certifications are an advantage. Knowledge of local labor laws and regulations in Ethiopia, with demonstrated ability to ensure compliance. Strong communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively across all levels of the organization. Proven ability to handle confidential information with integrity and professionalism, and to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. 1- 2 years experience ERP skill is plus",
