  {
    "title": "Tender assistant and Office messanger",
    "organization": "Huna General Trading",
    "description": "Company Description Huna General Trading is a growing trading company operating in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, with a focus on efficient commercial operations and client service. The company is involved in sourcing, procurement, and distribution of various goods to meet customer and partner needs. Huna General Trading values reliability, professionalism, and strong work ethics in its team members. The organization offers opportunities to learn different aspects of trading and office operations and encourages continuous improvement and collaboration. Role Description The Tender Assistant and Office Messenger is a full-time, on-site role based in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia. The role involves supporting the preparation, collection, and submission of tender documents, including organizing files, photocopying, printing, and ensuring all required documents are complete and submitted on time. The team member will deliver and collect documents from government offices, private institutions, and clients, and handle general office messenger duties such as banking errands, postal services, and document dispatch. The role also includes assisting with basic administrative tasks such as filing, record-keeping, and maintaining organized document archives. The position requires close coordination with the tender and administration teams, adherence to instructions, and professional communication with internal and external stakeholders. Qualifications Ability to read and speak English and Amharic Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to handle multiple tasks and meet deadlines. Basic administrative and clerical skills, including document handling, filing, photocopying, and record-keeping. Ability to follow procedures accurately, pay attention to detail, and maintain confidentiality of sensitive documents. Effective communication and interpersonal skills for interacting with colleagues, clients, and office staff. Reliability and professionalism in performing messenger duties, including timely and secure delivery of documents. Familiarity with local routes and offices in Addis Ababa, or willingness to learn and adapt quickly. Basic computer skills (e.g., using email, word processing, and simple document formatting) are an advantage. Previous experience in tender support, office assistance, or messenger work is preferred but not mandatory. Ability to work on-site full time and maintain a respectful, collaborative attitude within a diverse team.",
